id:                     E372
trigger_tool: conan|curl|python|buildbot
phase: download
error_signature: \[Errno 2\] No such file or directory: 'curl'|Can't connect to HTTPS URL because the SSL module is not available|Trying another mirror
severity: 3
category:               conan
match_keywords: Conan source, curl missing, Python SSL unavailable, HTTPS, HTTP mirror, authority mirror, sha256, conandata.yml, Buildbot
title: Hash-bound authority HTTP fallback for Conan workers without curl or SSL
root_cause: A worker can lack both curl and Python SSL while its CI pre-download parser also truncates hyphenated archive URLs, leaving Conan unable to fetch an HTTPS-only source even though the recipe and checksum are correct.
affected_scope: Conan recipes built on minimal workers where tools.files.get consumes conandata.yml after a best-effort CI pre-download step.
verification_cmd: Force the official HTTPS URL to fail in an isolated Conan home, require Trying another mirror, then verify RC0 extraction from a direct authority HTTP mirror with the exact official SHA-256.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: official-https-first-authority-http-fallback
rec_description: Keep the official HTTPS URL first, add only a direct byte-identical authority HTTP mirror second, retain one upstream SHA-256, and exercise the real Conan source fallback path.
rec_command: conan source <isolated-recipe> --output-folder <isolated-source-tree> -v
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: report-worker-infrastructure-blocker
fallback_description: If no qualifying authority HTTP endpoint exists, preserve the CI failure and repair the worker or shared downloader instead of weakening source integrity.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: url:.*http://(?!distfiles\.)|verify.*false|sha256: *['\"]?['\"]?$|sources:\s*url:\s*http://
forbid_1_reason: Arbitrary HTTP mirrors, disabled verification, missing hashes, or demoting the official HTTPS source remove provenance and integrity guarantees.
forbid_1_consequence: A compromised or drifting source can be accepted by CI and published as a trusted package.
principles:
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [E017, E299]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
doc_file: doc/E2149.md
last_updated: 2026-08-17
source_event: pkgconf 3.0.5 PR #5532 Buildbot #26293 buildid 29120
authors: 2301_80739235 <2047361658@qq.com>
